<title>USA: 4Kids Entertainment sees profitable year.</title>
<headline>4Kids Entertainment sees profitable year.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>4Kids Entertainment Inc said Friday that based in part on cost-cutting measures, it expects to be profitable for the full year 1996.</p>
<p>The projection is subject to &quot;reasonable market acceptance&quot; of new properties and characters represented by the company for licensing, it said.</p>
<p>Products licensed by the company include action figures based on its WMAC Masters weekly television show.</p>
<p>In the third quarter the company posted a net loss of $276,000, or $0.09 per share, on revenues of $995,000.</p>
</text>
